--TEST--
An enum in an enum body is `E0220`, an enum in a method body stays `E0233`, and an enum in a class body is accepted — `rule:enums/class-scoped-enum`, `rule:classes/a-type-is-declared-at-file-scope`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `rule:enums/class-scoped-enum`: an enum is declared at file scope or in a
// class or interface body, and nowhere else.
final class Accepted {
    enum Status { Open, Paid }
}

enum Outer {
    A,
    B,

    enum Inner { C }
}

final class InAMethod {
    public static function run(): void {
        enum Local { X }
    }
}

echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0220]: an enum is not declared in an enum body
   --> case.nvs:12:5
%A
error[E0233]: a nested `enum` declaration is not supported
   --> case.nvs:17:14
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
